rietta Materials (MLM). This chart runs from Sep 16, 2020 to Jan 25, 2021.","setup":"The stock rose about 38% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 4 weeks, peaking at $278.00 and pulling back 14% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Dec 3, 2020 it closed at $281.15, its first close above the base high of $277.41. Volume that day was 546K shares, 1.39x the prior 10-day average of 392K. It didn't hold. By Dec 11, 2020 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $308.00.","lesson":"This is an example of a shakeout. The breakout failed by the rules, closing below the level three days running, and then the stock recovered and ran. Cutting it was still the right call when it happened. A failed breakout that fixes itself is worth watching for a re-entry, not a reason to ignore the exit."}}